7. Advantages
-------------

✔ Removes if-else chains
✔ Open for extension
✔ Easy to add new algorithms
✔ Runtime algorithm selection
✔ Loose coupling
✔ Easier unit testing
✔ Better code reuse
✔ Follows SOLID principles

---------------------------------------------------------

8. Disadvantages
----------------

✘ More classes
✘ Client must know which strategy to select
✘ Slightly higher design complexity

---------------------------------------------------------

9. SOLID Principles Used
------------------------

✔ Open/Closed Principle (OCP)
Add new strategies without modifying existing code.

✔ Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP)
Context depends on the Strategy abstraction, not concrete classes.

